        "content": "#include <algorithm>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <utility>\n#include <vector>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nstatic const long long MOD = 1000000007LL;\n\nstatic long long modPow(long long base, long long exponent) {\n    long long result = 1;\n    while (exponent > 0) {\n        if (exponent & 1LL) result = result * base % MOD;\n        base = base * base % MOD;\n        exponent >>= 1LL;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int n, m;\n    if (!(cin >> n >> m)) return 0;\n\n    vector<pair<int, int>> obstacles;\n    obstacles.reserve(m);\n    bool blockedStart = false;\n    bool blockedEnd = false;\n    for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i) {\n        int row, col;\n        cin >> row >> col;\n        obstacles.emplace_back(row, col);\n        if (row == 0 && col == 0) blockedStart = true;\n        if (row == n - 1 && col == n - 1) blockedEnd = true;\n    }\n\n    if (blockedStart || blockedEnd) {\n        cout << 0 << '\\n';\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    sort(obstacles.begin(), obstacles.end());\n    obstacles.erase(unique(obstacles.begin(), obstacles.end()), obstacles.end());\n\n    const int maxSteps = 2 * (n - 1);\n    vector<long long> factorial(maxSteps + 1), inverseFactorial(maxSteps + 1);\n    factorial[0] = 1;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= maxSteps; ++i)\n        factorial[i] = factorial[i - 1] * i % MOD;\n    inverseFactorial[maxSteps] = modPow(factorial[maxSteps], MOD - 2);\n    for (int i = maxSteps; i > 0; --i)\n        inverseFactorial[i - 1] = inverseFactorial[i] * i % MOD;\n\n    auto pathsBetween = [&](int row1, int col1, int row2, int col2) {\n        int down = row2 - row1;\n        int right = col2 - col1;\n        int steps = down + right;\n        return factorial[steps] * inverseFactorial[down] % MOD * inverseFactorial[right] % MOD;\n    };\n\n    // Each predecessor contribution is independent. Batches of 64 keep the\n    // SIMD reduction sum safely below signed 64-bit overflow; obstacle order\n    // remains sequential because each ways[i] depends on earlier obstacles.\n    vector<long long> ways(obstacles.size());\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < obstacles.size(); ++i) {\n        const int row = obstacles[i].first;\n        const int col = obstacles[i].second;\n        long long total = pathsBetween(0, 0, row, col);\n\n        for (size_t begin = 0; begin < i; begin += 64) {\n            const size_t end = min(i, begin + 64);\n            long long partial = 0;\n#pragma omp simd reduction(+:partial)\n            for (size_t j = begin; j < end; ++j) {\n                const int prevRow = obstacles[j].first;\n                const int prevCol = obstacles[j].second;\n                if (prevRow <= row && prevCol <= col) {\n                    const long long contribution =\n                        pathsBetween(prevRow, prevCol, row, col) * ways[j] % MOD;\n                    partial += contribution;\n                }\n            }\n            total = (total - partial % MOD + MOD) % MOD;\n        }\n        ways[i] = total;\n    }\n\n    long long answer = pathsBetween(0, 0, n - 1, n - 1);\n    for (size_t begin = 0; begin < obstacles.size(); begin += 64) {\n        const size_t end = min(obstacles.size(), begin + 64);\n        long long partial = 0;\n#pragma omp simd reduction(+:partial)\n        for (size_t j = begin; j < end; ++j) {\n            const int row = obstacles[j].first;\n            const int col = obstacles[j].second;\n            if (row <= n - 1 && col <= n - 1) {\n                const long long contribution =\n                    pathsBetween(row, col, n - 1, n - 1) * ways[j] % MOD;\n                partial += contribution;\n            }\n        }\n        answer = (answer - partial % MOD + MOD) % MOD;\n    }\n\n    cout << answer << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n",
        "path": "src/solution.cpp"
      }
    ],
    "hypothesis": "Increasing the independent-predecessor SIMD reduction batch from 8 to 64 amortizes chunk-loop and modular-reduction overhead while preserving the sequential dependency between obstacles. The largest possible batch sum remains safely within signed 64-bit range.",
